    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1652">

                <pb facs="1307" n="1297" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg1297"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.8571/11–2149: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">McConaughy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-12-08T18:00:00-05:00">December 8, 1949—6
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2391. Stated urtel 4862 Nov 21 “Shanghai not yet faced problem registration
                    property”. Have Commie auths Shanghai issued reg[ulation]s re registration
                    property? If so or if auths shld do so, Dept assumes ConGen will tele
                    translation text regs.</p>
                <p>For ur info Dept has instructed ConGens Tientsin Peiping,<anchor n="61"
                        xml:id="d1652-f1"/> in connection with Commie regs requiring registration
                    real property of aliens those cities by certain dates, transmit to local Commie
                    auths statement reserving rights absentee Amer owners real property. Dept has
                    issued press releases giving this info.<anchor n="62" xml:id="d1652-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1652-f1" n="61" xml:id="d1652-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 764, November 2, 5 p.m., <ref target="#pg1113">p.
                    1113</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1652-f2" n="62" xml:id="d1652-f2-content">
                <p>See Department of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, November 21, 1949,
                    p. 760; November 1949, p. 800; December 5, 1949, p. 868a; December 26, 1949, p.
                    957.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
